# L §6.4: "Stacks are at most 4 deep and acyclic (LOAD-SCENARIO)": a over b, b over a.  Both refused; the base runs.
# Over the base of L6_4_scenario_stack (a gift of 100.00 PLN to each person monthly into konto) and its scenario
# child (a hypothetical child ola, a benefit move), with one change each.
=== household.tally
model household
  tally 2
  on 2026-10-20
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2030-12-31

source plan "plan"
unit PLN: currency minor 0.01
kind persons
kind gifts: event certain
  leg cash: PLN
place konto: accounts PLN lives 2019-05-01..
place world: outside lives 1900-01-01..
input gift_amt: money PLN
input gift_dom: int

move gift[m in months, p in persons on day_of(m, gift_dom)]: gifts
  on day_of(m, gift_dom)
  at start_of(m)
  leg cash from world to konto amount gift_amt

version plan_2026
  cite plan
  governs 2026..
  known 2026-01-01
  persons + [ana] lives 1990-04-02..
  gift_amt = 100.00 PLN "own"
  gift_dom = 5 "own"
  opening[konto] = 0 PLN at 2026-01-01 start "wyciąg"

ask c1: count(p in persons on 2027-06-01)
=== a.tally
scenario a over b
  tally 2
  from 2027-01-01
=== b.tally
scenario b over a
  tally 2
  from 2027-01-01
=== expect
scenario a: refused: LOAD-SCENARIO ...
scenario b: refused: LOAD-SCENARIO ...
c1: 1
  cut 2026-10-20
